{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>Slaughter a slaughter and prepare.</b> Like ״וְלִטְבֹּחַ טֶבַח וּלְהָכִין״ — and טְבֹחַ is not an imperative form, for it should have said וּטְבַח." "<b>At noon.</b> This is translated שֵׁירוּתָא — which is a term for the first meal in Aramaic, and in la'az דיזנ״ר. And there are many instances in the Talmud: שָׁדָא לְכַלְבָּא שֵׁירוּתֵהּ; בָּצַע אַכּוּלָא שֵׁירוּתָא — but every translation of צָהֳרַיִם is טִיהֲרָא."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 43, :notes {1 "The la'az דיזנ״ר corresponds to Old French disner, 'dinner' — the midday meal."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:22.566155803Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}